%N A234235 Denominators of minimum possible graph likelihood for a graph on n nodes.
%C A234235 The unique minimizer at n = 17 is obtained from C_5 by replacing its vertices, in cyclic order, by K_4, 4K_1, 4K_1, K_4 and K_1, with complete joins only between consecutive classes. This graph is self-complementary. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 28 2026
%C A234235 For n = 18 the minimum is attained, up to isomorphism, exactly by K_{9,9} and its complement. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 28 2026
%H A234235 Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="/A234235/b234235.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..18</a>
%H A234235 Simone Severini and Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19467">The minimum of the graph likelihood</a>, arXiv:2608.19467 [math.CO], 2026.
